<section>
  <exercises>
    <heading level="1">Section 3.2 Exercises</heading>
    <paragraph>Fill in the blank to make a true statement.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="69" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\sin^{2}x + \text{\_\_\_\_\_\_\_} = 1$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$cos 2 x cos 2 x$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="70" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\sec^{2}x - 1 = \text{\_\_\_\_\_\_\_}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <paragraph>Use an identity to reduce the power of the trigonometric function to a trigonometric function raised to the first power.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="71" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\sin^{2}x = \text{\_\_\_\_\_\_\_}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$1 - cos ( 2 x ) 2 1 - cos ( 2 x ) 2$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="72" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\cos^{2}x = \text{\_\_\_\_\_\_\_}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <paragraph>Evaluate each of the following integrals by u-substitution.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="73" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\int{\sin^{3}x\cos x dx}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$sin 4 x 4 + C sin 4 x 4 + C$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="74" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\int{\sqrt{\cos x}\sin x dx}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="75" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\int{\tan^{5}(2x)\sec^{2}(2x)dx}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$1 12 tan 6 ( 2 x ) + C 1 12 tan 6 ( 2 x ) + C$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="76" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\int{\sin^{7}(2x)\cos (2x)dx}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="77" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\int{\tan \left( \frac{x}{2} \right)\sec^{2}\left( \frac{x}{2} \right)dx}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$( x 2 ) x 2 + C 1 or sec 2 x 2 + C 2 ( x 2 ) x 2 + C 1 or sec 2 x 2 + C 2$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="78" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\int{\tan^{2}x\sec^{2}x dx}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <paragraph>Compute the following integrals using the guidelines for integrating powers of trigonometric functions. Use a CAS to check the solutions. (Note: Some of the problems may be done using techniques of integration learned previously.)</paragraph>
    <exercise number="79" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\int{\sin^{3}x dx}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$- cos x + 1 3 cos 3 x + C - cos x + 1 3 cos 3 x + C$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="80" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\int{\cos^{3}x dx}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="81" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\int{\sin x\cos x dx}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$-12cos2x+C-12cos2x+C$$ or $$12sin2x+C12sin2x+C$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="82" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\int{\cos^{5}x dx}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="83" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\int{\sin^{5}x\cos^{2}x dx}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$- 1 3 cos 3 x + 2 5 cos 5 x - 1 7 cos 7 x + C - 1 3 cos 3 x + 2 5 cos 5 x - 1 7 cos 7 x + C$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="84" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\int{\sin^{3}x\cos^{3}x dx}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="85" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$${\int\sqrt{\sin x}}\cos x dx$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$2 3 ( sin x ) 3 2 + C 2 3 ( sin x ) 3 2 + C$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="86" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$${\int\sqrt{\sin x}}\cos^{3}x dx$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="87" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\int{\sec x\tan x dx}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$sec x + C sec x + C$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="88" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\int{\tan (5x)dx}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="89" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\int{\tan^{2}x\sec x dx}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$1 2 sec x tan x - 1 2 ln ( sec x + tan x ) + C 1 2 sec x tan x - 1 2 ln ( sec x + tan x ) + C$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="90" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\int{\tan x\sec^{3}x dx}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="91" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\int{\sec^{4}x dx}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$2tanx3+13sec(x)2tanx2tanx3+13sec(x)2tanx$$ $$=tanx+tan3x3+C=tanx+tan3x3+C$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="92" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\int{\cot x dx}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="93" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\int{\csc x dx}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$- ln | cot x + csc x | + C - ln | cot x + csc x | + C$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="94" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\int{\frac{\tan^{3}x}{\sqrt{\sec x}}dx}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <paragraph>For the following exercises, find a general formula for the integrals.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="95" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\int{\sin^{2}ax\cos ax dx}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$sin 3 ( a x ) 3 a + C sin 3 ( a x ) 3 a + C$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="96" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\int{\sin ax\cos ax dx.}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <paragraph>Use the double-angle formulas to evaluate the following integrals.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="97" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\int_{0}^{\pi}{\sin^{2}x dx}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$\pi 2 \pi 2$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="98" has_solution="false">
