    <paragraph>For the following exercises, solve the differential equations.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="116" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\frac{dy}{dx} = \sin^{2}x.$$ The curve passes through point $$(0,0).$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="117" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\frac{dy}{d\theta} = \sin^{4}\left( {\pi\theta} \right)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$3 \theta 8 - 1 4 \pi sin ( 2 \pi \theta ) + 1 32 \pi sin ( 4 \pi \theta ) + C = f ( x ) 3 \theta 8 - 1 4 \pi sin ( 2 \pi \theta ) + 1 32 \pi sin ( 4 \pi \theta ) + C = f ( x )$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="118" has_solution="false">
